1
00:00:00,920 --> 00:00:01,220
Okay.

2
00:00:01,250 --> 00:00:02,360
So hello again.

3
00:00:02,630 --> 00:00:07,850
This is the second part of our lecture for QA specialists.

4
00:00:08,960 --> 00:00:18,800
And the first part was like more general about some terms and this would be, I guess, more useful

5
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:24,500
in your everyday work because here we will talk about GUI elements.

6
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:32,420
So how to call those things that you can see on those websites or in those apps.

7
00:00:32,420 --> 00:00:38,120
And it's important to know how they are called because there may be problems with them and then you

8
00:00:38,120 --> 00:00:40,100
have to describe them.

9
00:00:40,100 --> 00:00:45,140
So I believe that you'll find the names of those things really useful.

10
00:00:45,740 --> 00:00:47,420
Okay, let's start.

11
00:00:49,060 --> 00:00:54,460
So the first pair - check box and list box.

12
00:00:56,430 --> 00:01:00,930
All right, so checkbox is actually this box

13
00:01:00,930 --> 00:01:01,730
you can check.

14
00:01:01,950 --> 00:01:04,800
You check, you can put a tick there, like that.

15
00:01:04,800 --> 00:01:05,550
Right.

16
00:01:06,180 --> 00:01:14,610
And usually you can check a few things when we are talking about a checkbox and there is a list box.

17
00:01:14,790 --> 00:01:17,670
So this is actually a list of things, right?

18
00:01:17,670 --> 00:01:22,280
And again, you can choose not only one, but a few if you want.

19
00:01:22,560 --> 00:01:25,830
So you can select multiple things here.

20
00:01:26,790 --> 00:01:37,860
In this lecture, apart from these names, we've added also the sentences of possible problems with

21
00:01:37,860 --> 00:01:38,640
those things.

22
00:01:38,640 --> 00:01:45,210
So maybe if you have to write a bug report, right, to describe the problem, this could be useful.

23
00:01:45,210 --> 00:01:52,350
For example, when a user clicks the checkbox on the page, it doesn't check the actual box.

24
00:01:52,590 --> 00:01:56,090
It means when you click it, the tick doesn't appear.

25
00:01:56,100 --> 00:01:57,330
That's the problem.

26
00:01:58,380 --> 00:02:06,000
And when a user clicks, comma, it doesn't.

27
00:02:06,760 --> 00:02:07,440
Check.

28
00:02:07,480 --> 00:02:08,729
He doesn't do something.

29
00:02:08,740 --> 00:02:15,270
So you use a lot of those structures when you are describing problems.

30
00:02:15,280 --> 00:02:22,420
If a user does something or when a user does something, write things like that.

31
00:02:23,980 --> 00:02:29,170
The next one - impossible to select the forth item in the list box.

32
00:02:29,260 --> 00:02:32,020
Impossible to select the forth item.

33
00:02:34,390 --> 00:02:36,370
It's okay to omit it.

34
00:02:36,610 --> 00:02:38,260
Yes, it is a bad report.

35
00:02:38,260 --> 00:02:39,790
You are writing it quickly.

36
00:02:39,910 --> 00:02:45,520
Instead of saying it's impossible, you can just say impossible to select.

37
00:02:47,550 --> 00:02:48,390
Let's move on.

38
00:02:50,400 --> 00:02:52,740
And we move on to the next one.

39
00:02:52,740 --> 00:02:56,550
And here we have toggle and button.

40
00:02:56,880 --> 00:03:02,170
So let's start with toggle. Toggle is this kind of button.

41
00:03:02,190 --> 00:03:06,750
You can usually find it in your phones, I guess, right.

42
00:03:06,960 --> 00:03:09,840
So you click on it.

43
00:03:10,790 --> 00:03:14,540
To switch it to off or on position.

44
00:03:14,540 --> 00:03:20,240
So usually top toggle is about off on, switched on, switched off.

45
00:03:20,900 --> 00:03:22,580
And here is the example.

46
00:03:22,580 --> 00:03:27,230
That toggle button cannot be switched to off position, right?

47
00:03:27,230 --> 00:03:29,540
It cannot be switched to off position.

48
00:03:29,540 --> 00:03:34,010
So when I click on it, it doesn't change.

49
00:03:35,210 --> 00:03:37,370
And the next one is just a button.

50
00:03:38,270 --> 00:03:43,610
So this is a button here like this, for example, submit button.

51
00:03:44,300 --> 00:03:45,440
This blue one.

52
00:03:46,070 --> 00:03:48,800
They can be all types of buttons, right?

53
00:03:48,800 --> 00:03:51,470
So this is like the most general word, button.

54
00:03:52,010 --> 00:03:57,230
The style of submit button is different from the one in the mockup.

55
00:03:57,890 --> 00:04:04,610
So you can write the name of the button in capital letters to make it clear what button you refer to.

56
00:04:04,640 --> 00:04:06,020
Submit button.

57
00:04:07,340 --> 00:04:08,180
All right.

58
00:04:08,180 --> 00:04:10,280
Let's move on the next one.

59
00:04:11,800 --> 00:04:15,640
And we have radio button and drop down list.

60
00:04:16,120 --> 00:04:24,880
So a radio button, these types of buttons where you can also choose an option, the round ones.

61
00:04:25,060 --> 00:04:27,250
They are called radio buttons.

62
00:04:27,640 --> 00:04:31,570
The radio button is too small to click.

63
00:04:31,930 --> 00:04:33,730
Too big, too small.

64
00:04:34,900 --> 00:04:42,820
So usually with radio buttons, we can choose only one thing that's important that's different from

65
00:04:42,820 --> 00:04:46,000
what we had before, right.

66
00:04:46,090 --> 00:04:50,440
What we had with the checkbox, with radio button you can choose only one thing.

67
00:04:51,100 --> 00:04:55,030
Then we have dropdown list and drop down button.

68
00:04:56,400 --> 00:05:02,040
So this little thing is called a dropdown button.

69
00:05:03,230 --> 00:05:08,900
And if you click on a dropdown button, you can see a dropdown list.

70
00:05:08,900 --> 00:05:13,000
So it appears when you click on that little arrow.

71
00:05:13,010 --> 00:05:14,690
So here it's like open.

72
00:05:14,690 --> 00:05:18,740
So it's up, but usually it would be down.

73
00:05:18,740 --> 00:05:23,960
So then I clicked it and I can see the dropdown list.

74
00:05:24,730 --> 00:05:29,620
The dropdown list disappears when the user hovers over it.

75
00:05:31,760 --> 00:05:40,520
So all these words, we'll have a bit later. Hover over something like to move your cursor onto something

76
00:05:40,520 --> 00:05:48,670
like I'm hovering now over this list. OK, dropdown list and radio button 

77
00:05:48,680 --> 00:05:54,170
you can usually choose only one thing, only one option.

78
00:05:55,910 --> 00:05:57,200
All right.

79
00:05:57,200 --> 00:05:59,360
And we move on. Here

80
00:05:59,360 --> 00:06:03,230
we have text field and search field.

81
00:06:04,190 --> 00:06:05,180
Text field.

82
00:06:05,810 --> 00:06:09,810
So basically a place where you can type in text.

83
00:06:09,830 --> 00:06:15,260
It can be just a line of text or multiple lines of text.

84
00:06:15,770 --> 00:06:19,720
Often in some forms, this is from a Google form, right.

85
00:06:19,730 --> 00:06:23,870
So a place where you can type text.

86
00:06:25,190 --> 00:06:26,480
Here is an example.

87
00:06:26,690 --> 00:06:33,170
When a user types more than ten characters in the text field, the app crashes.

88
00:06:34,760 --> 00:06:38,420
I wanted to draw your attention to something.

89
00:06:39,900 --> 00:06:49,440
I find that a lot of people make this mistake when they describe some boxes, they forget this -s ending.

90
00:06:49,740 --> 00:06:54,390
Usually we talk about one user, a user types.

91
00:06:54,390 --> 00:06:56,370
We use present simple here.

92
00:06:56,610 --> 00:06:59,320
So don't forget about ending -s.

93
00:06:59,340 --> 00:07:11,250
As a user types, app crashes, we use present simple here and for he, she, it we have to use ending -s, please

94
00:07:11,250 --> 00:07:14,940
be careful. The next one search field.

95
00:07:16,260 --> 00:07:23,970
So here you can type things you want to find, you want to search like in Google for example, or on websites

96
00:07:23,970 --> 00:07:28,380
again, there are search fields that help you to navigate through that website.

97
00:07:29,410 --> 00:07:35,170
After refreshing search field, it's still filled with a previous search query.

98
00:07:35,560 --> 00:07:40,150
So the thing you're looking for is called search query.

99
00:07:40,180 --> 00:07:40,810
Yeah.

100
00:07:40,810 --> 00:07:43,930
And I just wanted to mention this thing.

101
00:07:44,730 --> 00:07:51,750
So search fields usually will be, you will usually see this thing in search fields.

102
00:07:51,780 --> 00:07:54,060
This is called magnifying glass.

103
00:07:54,840 --> 00:07:55,260
Right.

104
00:07:55,260 --> 00:07:56,640
Magnifying glass.

105
00:07:58,560 --> 00:07:59,490
The next one.

106
00:08:01,110 --> 00:08:02,280
Here we go.

107
00:08:02,670 --> 00:08:05,460
And placeholder.

108
00:08:06,390 --> 00:08:10,150
Kind of what we have here seems similar to a search field.

109
00:08:10,190 --> 00:08:16,920
Yes, there is a magnifying glass here as well, but placeholder means something that holds a place

110
00:08:16,920 --> 00:08:17,950
for something.

111
00:08:17,970 --> 00:08:20,990
So here it holds a place for that text.

112
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:27,150
And usually when you start typing that placeholder disappears.

113
00:08:28,740 --> 00:08:29,730
Okay.

114
00:08:29,820 --> 00:08:33,120
And the next word label.

115
00:08:33,900 --> 00:08:40,260
Label is like a title for that box, for example.

116
00:08:40,590 --> 00:08:42,230
Like, here, pick up,

117
00:08:42,240 --> 00:08:44,020
this is a label. Drop off,

118
00:08:44,039 --> 00:08:44,990
this is a label.

119
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:47,850
So this is a title for those boxes.

120
00:08:48,670 --> 00:08:48,940
Hmm.

121
00:08:49,650 --> 00:08:57,900
And another interesting thing, this gray text here type language, name or here location.

122
00:08:58,230 --> 00:09:04,200
So this is called hint text because it gives you a hint.

123
00:09:04,470 --> 00:09:05,910
What do you have to write?

124
00:09:06,510 --> 00:09:09,180
So this is this is called the hint text.

125
00:09:09,180 --> 00:09:12,900
And it usually disappears when you start typing again.

126
00:09:13,680 --> 00:09:14,920
Here is the example.

127
00:09:14,940 --> 00:09:19,260
The top left placeholder doesn't have a label.

128
00:09:21,570 --> 00:09:23,370
All right, let's move on.

129
00:09:24,690 --> 00:09:31,950
And here we'll talk about different groups, kind of like more navigational things that help you find

130
00:09:31,950 --> 00:09:33,120
things, right.

131
00:09:33,450 --> 00:09:36,510
Well, the first one here is toolbar.

132
00:09:37,410 --> 00:09:43,040
In different apps, you have different tools you can use to do different things.

133
00:09:43,050 --> 00:09:45,960
Well, this is obviously from PowerPoint, right?

134
00:09:47,330 --> 00:09:54,370
A toolbar, all those tools you can use and for example, the paste tool on the toolbar doesn't work.

135
00:09:54,380 --> 00:09:59,090
So if this button didn't work, I would say that the paste tool doesn't work.

136
00:09:59,630 --> 00:10:05,240
And often with those toolbars we have tool tips.

137
00:10:05,540 --> 00:10:10,470
So this is a short description of a tool that helps you to use it, right.

